\section{Methods}
% <><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><>
\begin{enumerate}
\item We used different data and models for budburst and seed germination.
\begin{enumerate}
\item We have complete (known chilling, forcing and photoperiod levels) data for 191 species for the budburst model, this data following the code used in MoralesCastilla \textit{et al}. 2024 publication, including removal of outlier species and correcting \textit{Acer pseudolatauns} for \textit{Acer pseudoplatanus}. %emwAug12 -- (1) ref the relevant code files here in the comments includingthe one i mentioned in the issue, and I often add any issue #s if they are especially relevant, (2) can you give the gymno/angio #s here also? (3) check my definition of complete is correct
\item We have complete data for 329 angiosperm species and 107 gymnosperm species for the seed germination model. %emwAug12 -- (1) ref the relevant code files here in the comments (2) define complete
\end{enumerate}
\item We modeled budburst as a function of forcing, chilling, and photoperiod, accounting for phylogeny: 

\[
\hat{y}_i = \alpha_{sp[i]} + \beta_{force,sp[i]} \cdot forcing_i + \beta_{chill,sp[i]} \cdot chilling_i + \beta_{photo,sp[i]} \cdot photoperiod_i
\]

where $sp[i]$ is the species of observation $i$, and species-level intercepts and slopes ($\alpha_{sp}$, $\beta_{\text{force},sp}$, $\beta_{\text{chill},sp}$, $\beta_{\text{photo},sp}$) are modeled according to species phylogenetic relationships.

\item We ran the model with forcing and chilling for seed germination considering phylogeny in the model %emwAug12 -- can we define how forcing and chilling were calculated? 

\item We modeled seed germination as a function of forcing and chilling, accounting for phylogeny, following the same structure as above (excluding the photoperiod term). The response variable was standardized to $[0,1]$ and modeled as an ordinal beta regression (with special handling for 0 and 1 observations). %emwAug12 -- here I would reference the R and Stan files currently used in the comments. 
    
\item After fitting both models, we extracted the species-level parameter estimates and compared the chilling and forcing effects on budburst versus seed germination for the 38 species overlapping between the two datasets. %emwAug12 -- how many gymnosperms and angiosperms? 
\end{enumerate}

